{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And they journeyed from Mount Hor by way of the Red Sea, to compass the land of Edom.</b> Because he did not let them pass through his land, they turned back seven stations, as the Rabbis of blessed memory mentioned from what is written (Deuteronomy 10:6): ״ובני ישראל נסעו מבארות בני יעקן מוסרה שם מת אהרן״ — and did he die in Moserah? Did he not die at Mount Hor? Rather, they turned back and eulogized him there."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:34:25.735333145Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}